Third-party components
----------------------

This repository contains Shijhon's own code and one third-party component:

- Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono (the dashboard's font), in
  src/shijhon/dashboard/static/fonts/ - Copyright 2020-2024 The Atkinson Hyperlegible
  Mono Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/atkinson-hyperlegible-next-mono),
  under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The license is the file OFL.txt in that
  folder. The font stays under the OFL.

Shijhon's runtime dependencies are not in this repository; they are installed from PyPI at
the versions uv.lock names. Two of them are under licenses other than permissive ones:

- mutagen (https://github.com/quodlibet/mutagen), the tagging library - GNU General
  Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version (GPL-2.0-or-later).
  Shijhon uses it under version 3, which section 13 of both licenses lets be combined
  with a program under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
- certifi (https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi), the CA bundle - Mozilla Public
  License 2.0 (MPL-2.0). Used unmodified.

The others are under permissive licenses, each with its license text in its own package:
aiolimiter, aiosqlite, annotated-types, anyio, async-lru, h11, pydantic, pydantic-core,
pydantic-settings and typing-inspection (MIT); click, httpcore, httpx, idna, Jinja2,
MarkupSafe, python-dotenv, Starlette and uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause); defusedxml and
typing-extensions (PSF-2.0).

Shijhon contains no code of Navidrome (GPL-3.0). It talks to an unmodified Navidrome over
HTTP and reads its database's contents; the Compose file names Navidrome's own image, which
this project does not distribute.


For whoever publishes a built image
-----------------------------------

This project publishes the Dockerfile, not an image. An image built from it holds, besides
Shijhon:

- the Python packages above, mutagen included: the image as a whole is then a work that
  combines Shijhon (AGPL-3.0-or-later) with mutagen (GPL), to be passed on under those
  licenses with its Corresponding Source: this repository at the commit that was built,
  with any changes (the Dockerfile and uv.lock, which the build follows, are in it), and
  the source of the Python packages in the image, mutagen's among them - each is on PyPI
  as a source distribution at the exact version uv.lock names;
- the base image python:3.12-slim-bookworm, at the digest the Dockerfile pins: CPython
  (PSF-2.0) and Debian 12 packages under their own licenses, GPL and LGPL ones among them
  (each package's terms are in the image under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright). The
  image's definition is at https://github.com/docker-library/python; Debian's source
  packages for the exact versions are at https://snapshot.debian.org/ and
  https://sources.debian.org/;
- Debian 12's ffmpeg and the libraries it needs, which the Dockerfile installs from
  Debian's archive (Shijhon runs it as a separate program to copy the audio of DASH
  links): Debian builds it under the GPL, and its libraries are under their own licenses,
  each in the image under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright; their source packages are at
  the same addresses.

Whoever distributes such an image names the base image and its digest, says where those
sources are, and keeps this file and LICENSE with it. The uv binary is used in the build
stage only and is not in the final image. docs/development.md ("Publishing an image") has
the commands that list the packages and fetch their sources.
